You generate `scripts/analyzer.py` (Python 3.10+).
Use ONLY local logic + the provided masters to compute one row for Google Sheets (existing 15 headers).
Inputs:
- argv[1] = path to transcript JSON (from transcriber), contains:
  transcript_text (str), segments[{t(str "MM:SS" or "HH:MM:SS"), speaker("OP"/"CUS"), text(str)}],
  file_meta{date?, phone?, filename, processed_at}
- config/ng_master.json, config/script_master.json, config/settings.json

Tasks:
1) Derive phone (10/11 digits, "0" start, no hyphen) from file_meta or filename "YYYY-MM-DD_XXXXXXXXXX_...".
2) Branch detection = first customer reaction -> one of {"#3-1","#3-2","#3-3","#3-4","MEDAPANI"}.
3) NG classification:
   - Extract NG candidates across #2/#3 portions via dictionaries and patterns from ng_master.json.
   - Define end-window: last 60s OR last 20% of call duration (choose max).
   - If candidates in window: pick the last by time; else pick last-highest certainty.
   - Certainty = utterance_strength + speaker_weight + explicitness + consistency (see spec_mvp.md).
   - evidence = [{t,speaker,text} 3 turns: prev, focal, next], and an excerpt <= 200 chars.
4) Talk-fit score (0..100): E1..E4 + Goal(day/time ask at turn end)=+20. strict=0.7 semantic.
5) Count rebuttals (see spec). Count schedule asks at end of #2/#3 turns. Compute lead days for each ask.
6) Phase time seconds for #1,#2,#3-1..#3-4 (sum of occurrences), integer seconds; total_duration from last seg.
7) Simple sentiment timeline per turn (lexicon-based or heuristic), triggers when polarity changes sharply.

Output (print to STDOUT, JSON object) covering sheet headers:
- "ファイル名": original filename
- "NG理由・断り文句": evidence excerpt (<=200 chars)
- "話者": guessed operator name or "—"
- "処理日時": file_meta.processed_at
- "ファイルID": use filename (or Drive ID if present in file_meta)
- "チェック内容": branch / notes
- "アポ取得タグ": e.g., "NG回避" or "—"
- "NG分類": "<major> > <minor>" (or "不明")
- "電話番号": normalized phone (or "不明")
- 残りの項目（会社名, 法人番号, HP, 大業種, 中業種, 従業員数）は空文字で出力

Constraints:
- No network calls. Robust to missing optional fields.
- Round floats to 2 decimals where needed, but final sheet row uses strings.
- Exit non-zero with helpful error on malformed inputs.

